      "slug": "doubanjiang",
      "term": "Doubanjiang",
      "definition": "A fermented paste made from broad beans and chillies, central to Sichuan cooking. It is salty, spicy and deeply savoury. Pixian county doubanjiang is considered the finest variety."
    },
    {
      "slug": "yu-xiang",
      "term": "Yu Xiang",
      "definition": "Literally 'fish-fragrant', this describes a Sichuan flavour profile built from garlic, ginger, spring onion, doubanjiang, vinegar and sugar. No fish is used despite the name."
    },
    {
      "slug": "rice-vinegar",
      "term": "Rice Vinegar",
      "definition": "A mild, slightly sweet vinegar brewed from fermented rice. It is less sharp than malt or white wine vinegar. Chinese rice vinegar is pale gold and used widely in sauces and dressings."
    }
  ],
